<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Piploda State</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Piploda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Rajput chiefship of western Malwa, long a dependency of the Nawabs of Jaora.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Piploda was held by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> Thakur family in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> from the late 18th century. When the British settled Malwa after 1818, it was placed under the Nawab of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jaora-state">Jaora</a> as a tributary holding.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakurs governed a few dozen villages and paid tribute to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jaora-state">Jaora State</a>. In the 20th century Piploda was separated from Jaora and placed directly under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa-agency">Malwa Agency</a>. Little else is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Piploda was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956; it lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ratlam-state">Ratlam</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/piploda-state.jpg" alt="Piploda State" width="320" height="498"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kesri_Singh,_Thakur_of_Piploda_in_1903.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Piploda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Piploda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=piploda-state" aria-label="Piploda State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6678 1308 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Piploda State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6998 1564L7364 1601M6998 1564L7364 1602M6998 1564L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6998 1564h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6998 1564h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=piploda-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
